<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Panama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1826</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Amphictyonic Congress</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Congress of Panama was a meeting of Spanish American republics called by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> and held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-city">Panama City</a> in June and July 1826 to form a league of the new states. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> attended, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>' delegates arrived too late and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> was not invited. Its treaty of perpetual union was ratified only by Gran Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-panama.jpg" alt="Congress of Panama" width="320" height="289" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagihuin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colombia_(Miranda)_y_Congreso_de_Panam%C3%A1_(Bol%C3%ADvar).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
